{%- comment -%}
  SYNOR — the free-delivery figure, for the tray's bar.

  sa-try-tray reads the threshold off the discovery box:

    var full = WK ? (tot >= WK.freeAt && picks.length > 0) : false

  The box was taken off this page, so WK is null, full can never be true,
  and the bar never reaches its gold state — the one moment the page is
  building towards. The figure was only ever carried in the box's data
  attributes, so it left with it.

  This carries it instead. The tray looks the element up document-wide
  ([data-stweek]) and guards every paint behind its own element lookups
  (WK.grid, WK.say, WK.fillEl, WK.pill, WK.spares), all of which are absent
  here, so drawWeek does nothing and drawBar gets its threshold back.

  Delete this the day the discovery box comes back, or the day the tray
  carries a free_at setting of its own.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div data-stweek hidden
     data-free="{{ free | default: 299 }}"
     data-rate="{{ rate | default: 49 }}"
     data-cur="{{ cur | default: '₹' }}"></div>
